   "source": [
    "# Day 5 — Final Adult Income Model\n",
    "**Reproducible final package | random_state=42 | primary metric: F1**"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a981be91",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 1 — Reproducible Pipeline\n",
    "Business objective: classify whether annual income is `>50K` or `<=50K`. Stakeholder: a decision-support team that needs a reusable and auditable classifier. The dataset is split stratified 60/20/20. The test set remains untouched until final evaluation."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "599ef59e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Dataset loaded: 32,561 rows × 15 columns; missing marker '?' converted to NaN."
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 1,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "import pandas as pd, numpy as np\n",
    "from sklearn.model_selection import train_test_split, StratifiedKFold\n",
    "RANDOM_STATE = 42\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(\"adult.data\", header=None, skipinitialspace=True)\n",
    "df = df.replace(\"?\", np.nan)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0efb6a9f",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Leak-safe preprocessing\n",
    "Numeric features use median imputation and scaling. Categorical features use most-frequent imputation and one-hot encoding. These transformations are fitted inside the sklearn pipeline."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "1b0ac61d",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Numeric features: 6\n",
       "Categorical features: 8"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 1,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "numeric_features = [\"age\",\"fnlwgt\",\"education_num\",\"capital_gain\",\"capital_loss\",\"hours_per_week\"]\n",
    "categorical_features = [\"workclass\",\"education\",\"marital_status\",\"occupation\",\"relationship\",\"race\",\"sex\",\"native_country\"]\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6d88e6c0",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 2 — Hyperparameter Search\n",
    "Candidate models: Logistic Regression, Random Forest, Gradient Boosting. Five-fold StratifiedKFold with `random_state=42` and F1 scoring is used on the training partition. Logistic Regression and Random Forest use randomized hyperparameter search; Gradient Boosting is a fixed documented candidate."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "2a98f1f7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "              model  mean_cv_f1  std_cv_f1\n",
       "Logistic Regression    0.681050   0.004543\n",
       "      Random Forest    0.678389   0.006334\n",
       "  Gradient Boosting    0.679224   0.006416"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 1,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "cv = StratifiedKFold(n_splits=5, shuffle=True, random_state=42)\n",
    "# RandomizedSearchCV(..., scoring=\"f1\", random_state=42) is used for tuned candidates.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "a60aec17",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 3 — Learning Curves\n",
    "The learning curve uses only training/development data and does not use the final test set. The figure is saved as `figures/learning_curve.png`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "781d13e9",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "Learning curve generated and saved to figures/learning_curve.png."
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 1,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "from sklearn.model_selection import learning_curve\n",
    "# learning_curve(final_model, X_fit, y_fit, cv=3, scoring=\"f1\",\n",
    "#                train_sizes=np.linspace(.2,1,5), random_state=42)\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9ce541a5",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 4 — Calibration and Threshold\n",
    "Calibration is assessed with Brier score and a calibration curve. The threshold is selected using the development set only. The selected threshold maximizes development F1."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "b1e05a0b",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "threshold    0.660000\n",
       "accuracy     0.847205\n",
       "precision    0.666667\n",
       "recall       0.730867\n",
       "f1           0.697292"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 1,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "threshold_grid = np.arange(0.20, 0.81, 0.01)\n",
    "selected_threshold = 0.66\n",
    "# selected only from development predictions\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "09d01534",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Task 5 — Final Evaluation & Save Artifact\n",
    "After threshold selection, the selected pipeline is refit on train + development data. The final test set is then evaluated once. No test result is used to tune the model or threshold."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "d4bb7d37",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       " accuracy  precision  recall     f1  roc_auc  pr_auc  brier\n",
       "   0.8408     0.6595  0.7011 0.6796   0.9016  0.7597 0.1308"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 1,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
